RE15pc — NOTICE
===============

This repository contains tooling, configuration and documentation only. It does
NOT contain, and must never contain, any Capcom code, art, audio, or disc data.

Running the port requires the user to supply their own copy of the Biohazard 2
(November 6, 1996) prototype disc image. That image is not redistributed here and
is excluded via .gitignore. The recompiled C# under generated/ is derived from
that disc at build time on the user's own machine and is likewise not
redistributed.


What this repository contains, verifiably
-----------------------------------------

Every file tracked here is plain text. That is not an assurance to be taken on
trust; it is a property anyone can check in one command:

    git ls-files | ForEach-Object { [IO.Path]::GetExtension($_) } | Sort-Object -Unique

The complete set of extensions is .cs .csproj .cue .editorconfig .gitattributes
.gitignore .json .md .patch .ps1 .sh .sln .yml - source code, configuration and
prose, and nothing else. The largest tracked file is a 125 KB function map, which
records addresses and symbol names rather than instructions or assets.

Explicitly not present, and excluded by named rules rather than by convention:

    the disc image           *.bin *.iso *.img *.chd *.mdf *.toc   .gitignore:13-19
    recompiled C# output     /generated/                           .gitignore:25
    VRAM, RAM and frames     /out/                                 .gitignore:28
    the upstream engine      /RecompOne/                           .gitignore:22

Those last two matter and are worth stating plainly. `/out/` holds the port's own
diagnostic dumps - raw video memory, a machine's RAM, and frame captures - and
those would contain decoded game art and overlay code if they were committed. They
are excluded for precisely that reason. The recompiled output under `/generated/`
is a transcription of the disc's executable and is excluded for the same reason.
Both are produced on the user's machine from the user's own disc, and neither is
distributed. All four rules can be verified directly:

    git check-ignore -v Bio2Nov96.bin generated/ out/ RecompOne/


If you are a rights holder
--------------------------

This project has no connection to Capcom, and it contains no game data. A takedown
notice needs to identify the material it concerns, and there is no such material in
this repository to identify - which the three commands above demonstrate rather
than merely assert.

If you believe something here is nevertheless a problem, please open an issue or
contact the repository owner. Concerns about this repository will be addressed
promptly, and the project's default position is to remove anything a rights holder
objects to rather than to argue about it.

Nothing in this file is legal advice, and it does not claim to be a defence against
any particular claim. It describes what the repository contains and how that can be
checked.


